# UST.G3DF H02 DM Source-Observation Corridor Theorem v1

## Status

`CLOSED_EXACT_H02_DM_SOURCE_OBSERVATION_CORE_AND_NO_STRUCTURAL_KERNEL_ZERO`

UST.G3DE emits the exact rank-`6,022` H02 factorization

```text
Delta_C = U S^-1 W.
```

UST.G3DF now locates the corresponding B89 inverse action inside the exact
H02 Dulmage-Mendelsohn condensation graph.

## Theorem

The `6,022` columns of `U` enter one DM component. The `6,022` rows of `W`
observe nineteen components. Intersecting the complete source-ancestor and
observation-descendant closures leaves exactly one component:

```text
the unique nontrivial H02 core, dimension 24,767.
```

Therefore the reduced coupling

```text
Q = W A0^-1 U
```

can be computed without traversing the full `42,458`-dimensional complement.
After a reduced vector is known, recovery of `A0^-1 U z` needs the core plus
`94` singleton ancestors, of total dimension `24,861`.

Unlike the H11 corridor, this graph has no structurally zero kernel rows or
columns. All `6,022` rows and all `6,022` columns of `Q` are source-observable.
Thus support alone cannot justify a smaller Woodbury kernel.

## Consequence

This result removes `17,691` complement directions from the H02 coupling
calculation and fixes the only large block that must be evaluated. It also
prevents an unproductive repeat of the H11 zero-column search: any further
reduction below `6,022` must come from coefficient rank or selected-state
reachability, not structural separation.

## Boundary

G3DF does not evaluate `A0^-1 U`, determine the rank of `Q`, construct the
source-dependent right-hand side, or integrate the path. It does not emit the
pairing-one rank-1,509 start class, the 248-row readout, or `beta_C`.

